1
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:21,560
Understood.

2
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:31,400
Shall I lower the altitude a bit more?

3
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,080
There's no need for that.

4
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:42,680
Leave the rest to you, Ryo-chan.

5
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:49,380
The helicopter from
before shot out our tires.

6
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,180
In that case, we'll escape on foot!

7
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,660
But this is an expressway, you know.

8
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:07,460
Sorry to keep you waiting, you villains!

9
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:09,080
Everyone's under arrest!

10
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:10,080
Come quietly.

11
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,460
Don't get scared just
because of a submachine gun!

12
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:23,080
They're an international syndicate.

13
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:24,460
If we keep dawdling,

14
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:26,740
we could drag civilians into this too!

15
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:28,920
Damn it!

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,200
I'll settle this in one go!

17
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:32,600
-You idiot!
-Maria!

18
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:33,040
Yes!

19
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,880
Bolmo and I will charge in! Cover us!

20
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:36,520
Roger!

21
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:38,300
Bolmo! Let's go!

22
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:39,300
Yaaah!

23
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:42,080
Go in and charge!

24
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:43,960
-Charge!
-Yes!

25
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:47,640
Bulletproof vests and helmets are no good!

26
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:48,820
Yaaah!

27
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:50,520
Woohoo!

28
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:56,280
Don't shoot!

29
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:57,340
Come on, get up!

30
00:01:58,440 --> 00:01:59,460
That was a piece of cake!

31
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,780
Help me!

32
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:03,100
Aaah!

33
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:04,880
Drop your guns!

34
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:06,980
Or I'll kill this guy!

35
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,920
W-there was another one?!

36
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,260
Help me!

37
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,000
What do we do? Those guys...

38
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:13,940
Leave this to me!

39
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,420
H-hey!

40
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:16,820
Senpai!

41
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:17,500
Ryo-sama!

42
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:22,640
Hey! Can't you hear us
telling you to drop your gun?

43
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,180
I can't hear a thing.

44
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:26,400
W-what?

45
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,200
Do you not care what
happens to this guy's life?

46
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:31,960
Do whatever you want with him,
boil him or grill him.

47
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:33,400
N-no way...

48
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:35,280
Stay back!

49
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:39,840
I see.

50
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:46,060
You call yourselves Special Security, yet -

51
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:56,400
We did it!

52
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,040
Come on, stand this one up.

53
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,260
Nice, Nakagawa!

54
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:00,820
Everyone's under arrest!

55
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,520
You're the one who was amazing, senpai.

56
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:06,660
W-wow...

57
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,960
We arrested everyone in one minute!

58
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,240
Like Ukkari Hachibei...

59
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:12,880
No...

60
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:15,460
My eyes, which chose Kankichi Ryotsu...

61
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:40,740
Next, member number 9.

62
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:43,600
Reiko Akimoto, Katsushika Station.

63
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:45,880
Well done, Chief.

64
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:48,300
Four members from our station were selected!

65
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:49,420
Hahaha.

66
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:52,780
Our station is full of talented people,
after all.

67
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,000
And the final member,

68
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:56,640
number 10, is

69
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,420
Kankichi Ryotsu.

70
00:03:58,420 --> 00:03:59,980
Katsushika Station.

71
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,320
Uuugh.

72
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,900
Uuugh.

73
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:05,700
Why is it Ryotsu?

74
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:07,620
No way.

75
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:09,880
That concludes the newly formed

76
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,120
Special Security

77
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,420
team, known as the SS Team.
Those are the members.

78
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:15,720
Now, to lead the team,

79
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:19,740
the captain of the world-famous SGS9,

80
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:22,120
Colonel Kepel will now say a few words.

81
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:28,660
Well, now that Tokyo has become
increasingly internationalized and high-tech,

82
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:32,400
in the near future, it is sure to experience

83
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:34,880
violent crimes and terrorism
like other international cities.

84
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:39,180
To prepare for that, we must quickly train

85
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:41,860
special forces like our nation's SGS9.

86
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:45,020
Colonel Kepel, I have a question.

87
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:46,400
What is it?

88
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:50,780
The last one chosen from our
station is a former Green Beret,

89
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:54,040
and Asato is a former kickboxing champion.

90
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:55,086
Nakagawa,

91
00:04:55,136 --> 00:04:59,380
Akimoto is one of the best
marksmen in the police force,

92
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:01,660
so I can see why she was chosen as a member.

93
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,400
But why did you choose Ryotsu?

94
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:08,420
Is it forbidden to choose Ryotsu?

95
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:12,980
Officer Ryotsu is a man who writes
over 100 incident reports a year.

96
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:16,120
There's no way he can handle
such an important mission.

97
00:05:16,740 --> 00:05:18,060
Tsk, tsk, tsk, tsk.

98
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:20,600
Ryotsu's shooting skills
are also first-rate.

99
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:24,000
He has outstanding vitality and energy.

100
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:28,060
And, just as every visiting party
needs a bumbling Ukkari Hachibei,

101
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:32,120
he's an essential vitamin for the SS team.

102
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:34,680
Y-you really know a lot about Japan,
don't you?

103
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:36,220
Yes!

104
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:49,960
Whoa! It's high!

105
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,040
Alright! Start the drop training!

106
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:54,580
Orugo Saigo, going!

107
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:59,140
One drop, two drop, three drop!

108
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:06,620
As expected of a former Green Beret,
impressive.

109
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:07,280
Next!

110
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,940
Ryotsu Kankichi, going!

111
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,340
One or two?

112
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,060
Aaaah!

113
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:16,340
Ugh, what what, aaaah!

114
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,180
R-Ryo-sama!

115
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,260
What are you doing, Ryo-chan!

116
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:24,820
Phew, I forgot to fasten my belt.

117
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:28,520
Hahaha, you're even worse
than Ukkari Hachibee, Ryotsu.

118
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:32,560
Be careful. There's a saying that
even gorillas fall from trees.

119
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:36,360
Colonel, if you're going to say it, it's
"even monkeys fall from trees."

120
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:36,580
Ahh -

121
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:40,740
Prime Minister, Prime Minister,
Prime Minister Hashimoto!

122
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:42,680
Ugh, how lame!

123
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:49,280
Colonel, being a Japan buff is fine,
but your gags are worse than Dave Spector's.

124
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:50,620
Is that so?

125
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:56,680
Next, regarding the tactics for when criminals
barricade themselves in a high-rise building...

126
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:04,480
I'm counting on you.

127
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,060
This is important training, so what's this?

128
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:10,600
Take a lesson from Ryotsu.

129
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:14,720
Look, he's not even blinking,
sitting up straight and listening properly.

130
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,160
Yes.

131
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:17,320
What's wrong with him?

132
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:20,420
Normally he's the first one to fall asleep.

133
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:21,660
He does seem strange.

134
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:22,980
Ryotsu.

135
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,800
If you were in this situation,
how would you arrest the criminals?

136
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:30,400
Ryotsu

137
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,120
Answer the question.

138
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:35,160
Ryo-sama

139
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:36,580
Gah...

140
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:38,960
Aaaaaah!

141
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:41,660
What on earth happened, ma'am?

142
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:42,420
Yocchan

143
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,120
It's a doll, you know.

144
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:51,820
It's a life-size figure a toy
maker made last year that never sold.

145
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:53,560
What the... Ryotsu?

146
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:01,500
Move that board aside.

147
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:02,340
Yes.

148
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:09,460
Ryotsu!

149
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:13,880
Idiot!

150
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:15,640
Go stand in the hallway.

151
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,940
It's not like you're some schoolkid
being made to stand in the hall!

152
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:22,920
Colonel Kepel.

153
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:25,580
Could I have a word?

154
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:26,340
What?

155
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:28,880
What did you say?

156
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:31,120
Everyone, the lecture is cancelled.

157
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:32,100
Ryotsu.

158
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:33,460
And Nakagawa too.

159
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:34,160
Akimoto.

160
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:34,860
Volvo.

161
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:39,000
Assemble in my room in 30 minutes.
Understood?

162
00:08:39,180 --> 00:08:39,540
Yes!

163
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:43,600
I wonder what happened?

164
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,940
The Colonel's face was pale.

165
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:49,100
Maybe he's gonna watch
some dirty videos with us?

166
00:08:49,760 --> 00:08:51,060
That's ridiculous!

167
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:53,287
Since the Colonel is a real Japan expert,

168
00:08:53,337 --> 00:08:55,940
maybe he'd be the chief of the Mito Kōmon Documents Section,
Onihei Squad?

169
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:58,150
I see. But,

170
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:01,560
if it were me, I'd recommend the
Dumb Lord of Shimura Prefecture.

171
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:07,940
Among the criminals we arrested last night,
there was a big shot.

172
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:11,840
This man, Adayada,
is the boss of a dark syndicate.

173
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:13,840
He's the younger brother of Abudarakatabura.

174
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,580
Abdullah Cadabra, you say?

175
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:19,680
You know him?

176
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:25,340
Yes. Wherever there's war or conflict, he sells weapons
and ammunition at high prices and makes a fortune.

177
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:26,860
He's an arms dealer on the black market.

178
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:31,000
He's internationally wanted,
yet has never once been caught.

179
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:32,660
He's the biggest of the big.

180
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,940
Abdullah Cadabra, then.

181
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:38,140
With a name like a magician's,
he doesn't look like a big shot.

182
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:40,760
Don't underestimate Abdullah.

183
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:44,100
He already knew about yesterday's arrest,

184
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:47,620
and he sent us a challenge letter.

185
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:48,960
A challenge letter?

186
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,240
Colonel Kepel.

187
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:54,680
How dare you arrest my brother!

188
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:58,480
You'll learn what happens when you defy me!

189
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:01,380
I will definitely get my brother back,

190
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:04,480
and I'll take revenge on
you and the entire SS team!

191
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:06,020
You'd better be prepared!

192
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:11,300
To send us a challenge like this,

193
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:13,300
he's got some nerve, hasn't he?

194
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:16,400
Take a look at this.

195
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:17,800
Who are they?

196
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:19,560
These scary-looking people?

197
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:23,680
Just now,
this was sent from SGS9 headquarters.

198
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:27,560
These are photos of the terrorists
Abdullah hired for revenge.

199
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,920
The leader, known as the
"Walking Destruction Man,"

200
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:32,120
Kalhendars.

201
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,600
A ruthless drill sergeant who bounced
from one foreign legion to another,

202
00:10:36,420 --> 00:10:38,220
he's a bomb specialist.

203
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:44,700
Next is former pro wrestler Atomic Thunder.

204
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:47,340
an expert in all martial arts.

205
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:49,700
A specialist in close-quarters combat.

206
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:52,160
Well, these two are

207
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:53,440
if we compare them to Mito Kōmon,

208
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:54,900
they're Suke-san and Kaku-san.

209
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,460
Next, Lily Francis.

210
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,060
There's a woman too?

211
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:01,040
Don't underestimate her
just because she's a woman.

212
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,860
Lily has won the Olympics

213
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:06,240
and world shooting championships,

214
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:09,000
sweeping the titles as
a shooting specialist.

215
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,620
If we use the Kōmon comparison,

216
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:13,680
she's in the Kagerou Oginn position.

217
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:17,140
Yumikaaru is far sexier, though.

218
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:20,140
And last, Gossha-sama Kosufuki.

219
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:23,060
A former sushi chef.

220
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:23,760
Sushi chef?

221
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,160
A foreigner being a sushi chef is unnatural,
isn't it.

222
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:34,140
He's Mongolian, half Russian and half American,
and his mother is British-Chinese.

223
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:39,900
That's no explanation at all. If you compare him to Kōmon-sama,
he's Kazaguruma no Yashichi.

224
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:42,360
Don't say anything more.

225
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:49,940
Anyway, all four of them would do anything for him.
They're terrorists who used to be mercenaries.

226
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:56,800
So far, we have no information that they've landed in Japan.
For now,

227
00:11:56,800 --> 00:12:01,020
Abdullah's brother will be secretly moved
from Kochi station to another location.

228
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:05,620
The plan is to round them all up in one
go while they're searching for his brother.

229
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:09,560
You two should also stand
by in case of an emergency.

230
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:11,360
Understood.

231
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,020
Under construction

232
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:04,040
What a terrible thing to do!

233
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,660
I never expected them to
already be here in Tokyo.

234
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,840
Hey, wrong way!
The airport is in the opposite direction.

235
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:16,920
This is fine.

236
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:19,280
Aren't we supposed to flee the country?

237
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:21,980
We were hired by your brother.

238
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:23,760
We don't take orders from you.

239
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:30,700
But we have a grudge against Kepel of SGS9,
who sent several of our comrades to prison.

240
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:35,060
Until we humiliate him,
we can't leave Japan.

241
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:40,460
Sergeant, I can see it now.

242
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:41,200
There it is.

243
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,420
Colonel Kepel

244
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,900
Station chief, Chief.

245
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:51,540
It's serious!

246
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:54,320
The terrorists who took
back Abdullah Cadabra

247
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,980
have stormed the Nakagawa
Information Center Building

248
00:13:56,980 --> 00:13:59,440
and are holding out inside with hostages.

249
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,520
What?!

250
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,040
That's not all.

251
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,360
Nakagawa, listen.

252
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,700
Listen carefully, with an open heart.

253
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:07,640
The hostage is your father.

254
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,480
No way.

255
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:11,640
We interrupt this program
to bring you a news report.

256
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,960
Around noon today, the Nakagawa
Information Center Building in Odaiba

257
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:17,640
was seized by unknown persons,

258
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:21,340
and company president Ryuichiro Nakagawa
is reportedly being held hostage.

259
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:24,860
and company president Ryuichiro Nakagawa
is reportedly being held hostage.

260
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:27,500
We now go live to the scene.

261
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:29,020
Reporter Kasai, at the scene.

262
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:35,660
Pulling off something this audacious,

263
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:40,340
you know the Japanese police and the
SS team won't just sit quietly, right?

264
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:41,800
That's exactly what we want.

265
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:46,320
Our standoff will be broadcast
around the world as news,

266
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:49,840
and everyone's eyes will be
glued to this Odaiba building.

267
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:54,220
More than ten news helicopters
are circling already.

268
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,040
I see.

269
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:58,880
We'll put on the greatest
show of all within that.

270
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:00,540
The greatest show?

271
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:05,080
Wes-on.

272
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,820
We've set up all the traps.

273
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:10,420
Especially on the first floor,
where we've planted plenty of explosives.

274
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:11,420
Let's send it.

275
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:20,860
Look at the amount of explosives we've got.

276
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:22,620
Perfect.

277
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:26,040
Then let's tell that
bastard Kepel our demands.

278
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:28,840
How much ransom are we asking for?

279
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,100
10 billion yen.

280
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:32,320
10 billion yen, did you say?

281
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:35,000
That's an amount the Nakagawa
conglomerate can pay, right?

282
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,100
Even so,
10 billion yen is too expensive, isn't it?

283
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,980
Who said it's expensive?

284
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:42,040
10 billion yen is too cheap.

285
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:42,580
What?

286
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:45,860
I'm a man who earns 100
million yen every second.

287
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:49,760
If we're released from the hostage
situation for such a paltry ransom,

288
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:51,020
we'll be a laughingstock.

289
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:54,380
Make it one trillion yen.
No, ten trillion yen!

290
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:57,400
Ten trillion yen?

291
00:16:04,020 --> 00:16:06,920
Ten trillion yen and a
plane to flee overseas?

292
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:10,500
Those are the terms the terrorists demanded?

293
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,561
That's right.
If we don't have it ready by 3 p.m.,

294
00:16:13,611 --> 00:16:15,720
they say they'll kill Nakagawa Ryuichiro.

295
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,040
For now, let's get it arranged.

296
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,660
Hey, hey, wait a minute!

297
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:21,300
Ten trillion yen is

298
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:24,940
a hundred, a thousand,
ten thousand times my salary,

299
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:27,940
that's more than I can
even wrap my head around!

300
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:30,880
As expected of the
world's Nakagawa zaibatsu.

301
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:34,200
In the old days, that would've bought
you a country like Kinokuni or Munjaemon.

302
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:37,520
You two, storm in through the back entrance.

303
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:38,080
Understood.

304
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,080
The rest of us will break through the front.

305
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:40,680
Understood.

306
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:57,380
Looks like a rat already got caught!

307
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:00,680
This must be the direct route
to the president's office.

308
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:01,720
Wait, Ryo-chan!

309
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:04,060
Everyone, fall back!

310
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:06,320
Hey, what do we do, Reiko?

311
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:23,000
Damn, even traps like this!

312
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,660
If Reiko-san hadn't stopped us,
we'd all have been taken out.

313
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:29,460
Damn, looks like we've got no
choice but to climb the stairs.

314
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:36,080
There are infrared beams set up here too.

315
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:40,700
If we can't even get past the stairs,
we'll never reach the president's office.

316
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:44,980
Don't worry, it's an eye for an eye,
a bomb for a bomb.

317
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:48,480
We've got Bolgo, the walking bomb.

318
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:50,700
Leave the bombs to me.

319
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,580
Why did you bother changing clothes?

320
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:02,760
Besides, Woodland camouflage only makes
you stand out more inside a building.

321
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:05,840
It's fine, they'll take the bullets for us.

322
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:12,520
Come out, you bastards!

323
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:23,000
As expected of an ex-Green Beret.

324
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,520
Let's keep moving forward!

325
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:28,840
But the scary part is that they don't
even check whether there are people there.

326
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:31,540
There's no telling friend from foe,
is there?

327
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,360
We can't move any further from here.

328
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,940
How many enemies were there?

329
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:42,840
No, I used up all the grenades I had.

330
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:45,920
Eight! Think about the
number and use them wisely!

331
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:50,940
This time it's fine, I brought all I had.

332
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:52,780
Are you Gonbe or something?

333
00:18:52,780 --> 00:18:56,200
If we get shot from behind,
the whole building will blow up.

334
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,840
Demons out!

335
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:01,580
Soccer-style shooting!

336
00:19:03,220 --> 00:19:05,240
Good, Porumon, keep it up!

337
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:07,580
Demons out!

338
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:17,960
You idiot! What are you going to do, blow up the stairs?
You're using way too many!

339
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:21,440
But just in case, for safety's sake,

340
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:26,060
Don't use ten at a time! Are you
doing dynamite demolition or something?

341
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:29,500
S-sorry, I'll be more restrained.

342
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,780
Restrained, restrained.

343
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,100
Yo-you... you bastard!

344
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,920
Are you trying to wipe out our own side?

345
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:49,600
I just can't get into the
groove unless I go all out.

346
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:50,440
That's enough.

347
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:51,980
Nakagawa, do it.

348
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:52,680
Yes!

349
00:19:55,140 --> 00:19:59,140
Looks like they've got a bomb guy
just like the sergeant over there, too.

350
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:01,780
I never expected them to climb halfway up.

351
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:03,740
Thunder Gossha!

352
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:05,280
Your time to shine has come.

353
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:17,060
Nakagawa's really going all out, isn't he.

354
00:20:17,570 --> 00:20:19,800
Dad wants to save him
with his own two hands.

355
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,460
Yeah!

356
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,760
Alright! Don't let Nakagawa get ahead of us!

357
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:26,600
Dad, I'll definitely rescue you.

358
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:33,340
Whoa! Nakagawa!

359
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,060
Stop it!

360
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,580
Make him do it that way.

361
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:01,800
No way.

362
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,360
Volko, with a single blow.

363
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:04,940
What monstrous strength!

364
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:08,020
This is the end for you too.

365
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:31,240
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

366
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,480
I'll be your opponent.

367
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:38,440
Alright.

368
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:41,820
If we follow this...

369
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:00,800
Hey! That's far enough!

370
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:04,060
Stop, or I'll kill this woman!

371
00:22:04,060 --> 00:22:04,740
Kei-chan.

372
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:06,800
Reiko-san.

373
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:16,080
Is it a dead end up there?

374
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:19,020
So, Reiko is...

375
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:21,160
This must be the president's office.

376
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:25,900
Looks like just the two of
them took care of everything.

377
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:27,200
Keiichi.

378
00:22:29,020 --> 00:22:29,420
What?

379
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:34,160
Stay still and behave!

380
00:22:35,220 --> 00:22:37,080
Hey, Mister Ryotsu!

381
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:38,560
Hey!

382
00:22:38,660 --> 00:22:40,800
Is Nakagawa's old man all right?

383
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:42,560
You bastard!

384
00:22:42,940 --> 00:22:46,480
Heh, the match is over,
so everyone raise your hands!

385
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,380
It's you who's raising your hands, punk!

386
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:48,980
What?

387
00:22:52,180 --> 00:22:53,220
S-senpai!

388
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:54,440
Nakagawa!

389
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:55,600
Keichi...

390
00:22:55,600 --> 00:22:56,220
Dad!

391
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:58,180
You got caught, didn't you!

392
00:22:58,540 --> 00:23:01,400
Sorry... I'm sorry...

393
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:04,040
All of you

394
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:05,380
I'm sorry!

395
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:07,600
Looks like the tables have turned.

396
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:09,000
Hey

397
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:14,520
Is this really all Japan's SS can manage?

398
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:17,860
Pathetic,
unable to beat just the four of us.

399
00:23:17,860 --> 00:23:20,340
Shut up! These are just the backup troops!

400
00:23:20,620 --> 00:23:22,860
I'll bring the real ones,
so you wait right there!

401
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:25,200
Everyone! We'll definitely save you!

402
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:30,300
No way!
This is the 100th floor of the building!

403
00:23:30,300 --> 00:23:33,460
Right, I forgot it was the 100th time.

404
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,360
What a fool.

405
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:42,580
Only Kepel's left

406
00:23:42,580 --> 00:23:44,880
He's not the kind of
senior who dies from this!

407
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:46,340
That's right.

408
00:23:46,340 --> 00:23:49,420
Gyō-chan's life force is tougher than a cockroach's,
after all.

409
00:23:55,440 --> 00:24:01,080
Ugh, you put me through this! You'd
better remember what you've got coming!

